<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">June 8, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 101</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-06-08T09:00:00+02:00</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v47.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL (written LAST by Judge) ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      <span class="cite">F1</span> löste YES på IRGC:s beslutande av "Arista" — den konkreta eskaleringsåtgärd som forecast-frågade om — medan <span class="cite">F4</span> föll 17pp (till 28%) och <span class="cite">F5</span> föll 18pp (till 12%) på direkta Iran-Israel-missiltväxlingar juni 6-8 som fördjupade det diplomatiska och maritima gapet; <span class="cite">F7</span> steg 20pp (till 55%) på retroaktiv söndagsöversyn av 106-0-upplösningsrösten.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">7 active · 3 resolved today (F1 YES · F2 NO · F3 NO) · last reasoned 2026-06-08</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-Term · ≤72h</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 Days</div>

      <!-- F10 — June 14 — military -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Israel and Iran exchange direct missile or drone strikes (not proxy) at least once more before EOD 2026-06-14?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">72%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast · prior 72% (2026-06-08)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-06-14</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Tit-for-tat pattern since June 6: IRGC drones toward Strait (June 6) → CENTCOM strikes Iranian radar (June 6) → Iran fires missiles at Israel (June 7) → Israel strikes central/western Iran (June 8). This 72-hour cadence establishes a high base rate for continued direct exchange within 7 days. US pressure on Israel and Iran's incentive to keep the ceasefire nominally alive provide a partial brake.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a named TIER1 source reports at least one confirmed direct missile or drone strike from Israel targeting Iranian territory OR from Iran targeting Israeli territory between 2026-06-08 and 2026-06-14.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 OR one TIER1 + CENTCOM/IDF official confirmation.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Proxy attacks (Hezbollah, Houthi, IRGC proxies) do NOT count. US strikes on Iran do NOT count. Only direct Israel↔Iran territory strikes qualify.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM/IDF confirmation of direct Israel-Iran strike</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Reuters/AP report of Iranian missile launch at Israel</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F8 — June 15 — military -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the April 2026 Iran-US ceasefire framework remain nominally in effect (no formal US or Iranian declaration of ceasefire termination) through EOD 2026-06-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">55%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast · prior 55% (2026-06-08)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-06-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Ceasefire under acute strain: Iran fired missiles at Israel June 7; Israel struck central/western Iran June 8; CENTCOM hit Iranian radar sites June 6. Neither side has formally declared termination as of June 8. Iranian state media stressed right to respond "at a time and place of Iran's choosing" without declaring ceasefire ended. Both sides retain incentives to avoid formal breakdown (oil markets, sanctions leverage). 55% reflects the ceasefire label may persist even under active strikes.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if both US and Iran refrain from formally announcing termination of the April ceasefire framework through EOD 2026-06-15. NO if either the US President/SecDef or Iranian Supreme Leader/President formally declares ceasefire ended or announces resumed war operations.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP) OR one TIER1 + official US or Iranian government statement confirming termination.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Continued military strikes WITHOUT a formal ceasefire-termination declaration = YES. If ambiguity exists about whether strikes constitute formal termination, RESOLVE-AMBIGUOUS-AS-YES.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US formal announcement of ceasefire termination</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iranian Supreme Leader or President declares ceasefire ended</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F4 — June 16 — diplomacy -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran resume negotiations with the US before EOD 2026-06-16?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −17pp from 45% (2026-06-02)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-06-16</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran suspended mediator-channel talks June 1. FM Araghchi confirmed "no significant progress" as of June 8; Iran's gate condition (full halt to Lebanon fighting) receded as Hezbollah rejected the Israel-Lebanon ceasefire on June 4. The June 6-8 Iran-Israel-US missile exchanges (Isfahan strikes June 7-8, CENTCOM radar strikes June 6) deepened the diplomatic gap. Pakistan's Naqvi conducting back-channel message-brokering — assessed as message-exchange, not formal negotiations. Trump's "rapid pace" assertion excluded per ambiguity rule. DA opposing narrative accepted; Isfahan strikes June 7-8 justify additional reduction.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if an Iranian official or state media (IRNA/Tasnim/Fars) confirms negotiations resumed, OR a named US/mediator official (Oman, Qatar, or Pakistan MFA) confirms Iran re-engaged, before EOD 2026-06-16.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two independent TIER1 OR one TIER1 + official Iranian state-media.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Trump-only assertions do NOT count. Pakistan Interior Minister relays are message-brokering, not negotiations, unless MFA explicitly characterises them as resumed talks. Indirect exchanges not called negotiations = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iranian MFA spokesman confirms re-engagement</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Omani/Qatari/Pakistani MFA mediator readout of resumed session</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F5 — July 2 — market -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Hormuz reach ≥50 commercial transits/day (7-day avg) before EOD 2026-07-02?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">12%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −18pp from 30% (2026-06-02)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-02</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Traffic at ~10 commercial transits/day (11% of baseline). June 6-8 saw IRGC seize the "Arista" vessel, direct Iran-US-Israel missile exchanges, and CENTCOM strikes on Iranian coastal radar. No demining announced. Pakistan back-channel yielding "no significant progress." The 60-day MOU remains unsigned. Fitch projects reopening no earlier than July. Reaching 50+ transits/day (7-day avg) by July 2 requires formal agreement, demining, and traffic resumption within 3 weeks against deteriorating ceasefire conditions.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch (or equivalent AIS) records ≥50 commercial transits/day averaged over any consecutive 7-day window between 2026-06-02 and 2026-07-02.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IMF PortWatch + one TIER1/OSINT shipping report (Bloomberg/Reuters/Lloyd's List).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Dark-fleet/Iranian-flagged-only transits with Western insurers refusing = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. PGSA addendum: PGSA self-reported figures excluded; ≥2 independent sources required for PGSA-regime vessels. Naval-escorted convoys count if independently verified by AIS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IMF PortWatch 7-day avg ≥50 transits</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Formal MOU signed enabling reopening</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

      <!-- F9 — July 15 — market -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz reach ≥25 daily transits (7-day avg) before EOD 2026-07-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">20%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast · prior 20% (2026-06-08)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast replacing expired F3 (June-10 node) with a lower-threshold partial-reopening signal. Current traffic ~10/day. Even partial demining and an interim MOU could push daily transits to 25+. At 20%, reflecting long odds given current military escalation spiral, unsigned MOU, and absence of any demining announcement.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch, UNCTAD, or Lloyd's List/Bloomberg AIS records ≥25 commercial transits/day averaged over any consecutive 7-day window between 2026-06-08 and 2026-07-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1 shipping-data source (IMF PortWatch/Bloomberg AIS/Lloyd's List) with explicit 7-day-average figure.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Iranian-claimed transits without independent AIS corroboration do not count. Dark-fleet-only without Western insurer participation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. PGSA self-reported excluded; ≥2 independent sources required for PGSA vessels.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IMF PortWatch 7-day avg ≥25 transits</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US-Iran interim MOU signed enabling demining</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F6 — July 15 — domestic -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F6</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Knesset pass the dissolution bill's final reading with an election date earlier than 2026-10-27 before EOD 2026-07-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">50%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 50% (2026-06-02)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">No second or third reading since the June 2 first reading (106-0). House Committee advanced bill without inserting an election date. Haredi parties maintain September preference; Netanyahu prefers October; no concession from either side this week. July 15 horizon gives approximately 5 weeks for remaining readings plus date-setting. No material movement.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the Knesset passes the dissolution bill in final (third) reading specifying an election date earlier than 2026-10-27, before EOD 2026-07-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Times of Israel/Reuters/AP) citing the Knesset plenum vote record.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>First/second readings without final passage do NOT count. If bill passes but sets date on/after Oct 27, resolve NO. If passage occurs but date left to later committee, AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Plenum third-reading dissolution vote held</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Haredi-coalition agreement on a September date</span>
        </div>
